e energy consumption of an average household increases by $1\\,\\text{kWh}$ every week. What differential equation describes the rate of change of energy consumption $E(t)$ (measured in $\\text{kWh}$) of an average household during these months? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in weeks." :question/worked-solution "If the energy consumption of an average household is $E\\,\\text{kWh},$ then the rate of change of the energy consumption is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in weeks.\n\nSince an additional $1\\,\\text{kWh}$ is consumed every week, the rate of change of the energy consumption is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection/68ec0c303d24b6a00c541ba1b08613cb7f26dba0c5b1cc541d477a6928bb35c2" :answer/id #uuid "af92d1b9-2507-5e94-9abd-fb632d45b1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=P-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection/b937f0d97bfffce9782a0fcbbb49b4f9c0c4684b7b98b9b9ccae65933b7320f4" :answer/id #uuid "ba2d3d44-c6a4-552b-af23-bf2cc078ffa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-6P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection/0336fdc3a95df10f9601ad665a6c3ae115b0e1417c32222c7f12ceb744dedab7" :answer/id #uuid "ce12ebed-a77d-55f7-90f8-22c5b9dfbf8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection/5a654db998cc96861a864c9c1dfef6f2639684e2bc5e4a5ef9f27b96804a3338" :answer/id #uuid "821be48c-6c28-599a-a1df-cf3418d1bb86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=6P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection/7fdb4c706a2dc10e0f852319e8819562710e55f676ba8d9bb4e209743e67c7d5" :answer/id #uuid "fa3d769c-c627-57a0-b301-05bcabe5649d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5108b9bd-46b0-53ff-a9c8-fbd4081c54ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119053/selection/0336fdc3a95df10f9601ad665a6c3ae115b0e1417c32222c7f12ceb744dedab7" :answer-field/choices ["q-119053/selection/68ec0c303d24b6a00c541ba1b08613cb7f26dba0c5b1cc541d477a6928bb35c2" "q-119053/selection/b937f0d97bfffce9782a0fcbbb49b4f9c0c4684b7b98b9b9ccae65933b7320f4" "q-119053/selection/0336fdc3a95df10f9601ad665a6c3ae115b0e1417c32222c7f12ceb744dedab7" "q-119053/selection/5a654db998cc96861a864c9c1dfef6f2639684e2bc5e4a5ef9f27b96804a3338" "q-119053/selection/7fdb4c706a2dc10e0f852319e8819562710e55f676ba8d9bb4e209743e67c7d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119053" :question/id #uuid "ac92dfbf-ccb9-575c-9ce8-ae4ff8a7a4a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-119053" :question/problem "Lucy reads $6$ pages of her new book each day. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of pages $P(t)$ Lucy has left to read? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days." :question/worked-solution "If the number of pages Lucy has left to read is $P$, then the rate of change of the number of the pages is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Lucy reads $6$ pages every day, the rate of change of the number of pages she has left is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-6.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the number of pages Lucy has left to read is *decreasing*." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38595"] :question/problem "Peter has planted a tree. The height $h$ of the tree increases at a rate that is proportional to the height of the tree. What differential equation describes the rate of growth of the height of the tree at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** of the tree **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **height** of the tree.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *height.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}∝h.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=kh.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection/74ad83bf45fdfc3dd9468e5f5c4e0e4ee351bdead489bd6c7ae00836e67513d4" :answer/id #uuid "1e7230c3-5b17-5ad4-964f-a41bc3794ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection/32fb54a3131da38e75fa482fda87c74dc3f9edaa593126c91abf9c23df7059de" :answer/id #uuid "2684a100-c840-5ef6-935a-64b1ec4dfd43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection/9f1e9de73fa6f93a0fef31ae0f8baed6a853a3261437aa07ac5a52ef3823fac5" :answer/id #uuid "cf60eb93-3667-5bd5-8af4-3f31821f3038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection/d926fcca1bf87ec8be3338b3888eda9d862313126e919d4f2ebcfd7ef2629cca" :answer/id #uuid "23426d91-83f7-5fd3-9d59-5571f7871632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{V},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection/d9083c443bffdb906b79f7a2c0d4feebc38aa72f548bf00a8b4d0ebd09e77184" :answer/id #uuid "73970c12-cb49-5223-aecf-0749c9c672ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f253a80-dc2e-5c9b-a29b-27ebd873e264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143034/selection/d9083c443bffdb906b79f7a2c0d4feebc38aa72f548bf00a8b4d0ebd09e77184" :answer-field/choices ["q-143034/selection/74ad83bf45fdfc3dd9468e5f5c4e0e4ee351bdead489bd6c7ae00836e67513d4" "q-143034/selection/32fb54a3131da38e75fa482fda87c74dc3f9edaa593126c91abf9c23df7059de" "q-143034/selection/9f1e9de73fa6f93a0fef31ae0f8baed6a853a3261437aa07ac5a52ef3823fac5" "q-143034/selection/d926fcca1bf87ec8be3338b3888eda9d862313126e919d4f2ebcfd7ef2629cca" "q-143034/selection/d9083c443bffdb906b79f7a2c0d4feebc38aa72f548bf00a8b4d0ebd09e77184"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143034" :question/id #uuid "b30d46be-646e-5361-a604-5fb66c710b5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143034" :question/problem "The value $V$ of a particular art object increases with time. The rate of change of the object's value is proportional to the square of the value. What differential equation describes the change of the value at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **value** $V$ of a particular art object **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the object's value is **proportional** to the **square of the value**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *value* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *value squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝{V}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection/51167820da5d3f06f05b4dafc3dbf6ca2a9da080bcebdc905bbcad91c8a97171" :answer/id #uuid "8028e7e8-3b3b-504d-ba91-f836d9cb7c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection/254452d02215b452595395ab011bc52010dcb750a22cebc3dc8722638e1405c9" :answer/id #uuid "58a97aba-52e7-5dc6-9464-3f0c8f478328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection/6a6d2dfa0ba1fe62c6a99b2f1ebea941fbfa580092713d5679fd1070365d6739" :answer/id #uuid "22454eb9-32f0-562a-a6d6-34138d61dbee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection/04471db144b3d7e5d438876e9d9d02ab84ed966a86cc845d0e78593c89c18838" :answer/id #uuid "cd86361b-c2b2-57c1-8939-9d91a4174c60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection/80f96a6baa353d7c6facbab39490b00c553de81005b205205d4be23ffd5e2cab" :answer/id #uuid "444c2823-b849-5936-a4d8-fe451fc18875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18d74731-e3b8-56d6-ac10-f73636d8a859" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143031/selection/04471db144b3d7e5d438876e9d9d02ab84ed966a86cc845d0e78593c89c18838" :answer-field/choices ["q-143031/selection/51167820da5d3f06f05b4dafc3dbf6ca2a9da080bcebdc905bbcad91c8a97171" "q-143031/selection/254452d02215b452595395ab011bc52010dcb750a22cebc3dc8722638e1405c9" "q-143031/selection/6a6d2dfa0ba1fe62c6a99b2f1ebea941fbfa580092713d5679fd1070365d6739" "q-143031/selection/04471db144b3d7e5d438876e9d9d02ab84ed966a86cc845d0e78593c89c18838" "q-143031/selection/80f96a6baa353d7c6facbab39490b00c553de81005b205205d4be23ffd5e2cab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143031" :question/id #uuid "95e26d6b-7e34-50c6-b783-26e5d7040c15" :question/math-academy-id "q-143031" :question/problem "The number of sales $S$ of a particular book increases with time. The rate of change of the number of sales is proportional to the square of the number of sales. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of sales of the book at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of sales** $S$ of a particular book **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the number of sales is **proportional** to the **the square of the number of sales**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of sales* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of sales squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}∝{S}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of sales *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143031/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection/43cccfa7afd1786868b5663386d0851eab374d8c0f6befd3946896f45ba661d0" :answer/id #uuid "d23ea2a3-f89e-574d-bfb0-56e39f72adba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k+\\frac{1}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection/b72dd9697f49385ccc5e5960ffb4cca18179ab08897d5d50eda25d57fed380f3" :answer/id #uuid "b50f87fe-bd0e-5f67-a879-df8f18b948ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{B}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection/c10de62d8125dd952ae2853436204c7ac91ef2cf9c24ef921872a8506d65eb0b" :answer/id #uuid "ae957a24-975a-515d-a05e-0bf046ea696c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k-\\frac{1}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection/0a699f5e222b2541cc0b57d0909108bee4edcc63642004a89241b5631a6dad5d" :answer/id #uuid "25897e8d-b758-5a76-8f52-e2842d06d3a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{t}{B}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection/468dcf99a9303f0cd266be5aacdd9f165d173bb1ea34766d371a1a380255f0c5" :answer/id #uuid "3c3be60f-7d3d-5c25-8e1a-2e04879ed5b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aef1a381-71aa-5859-8fa4-51baa76310af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38596/selection/468dcf99a9303f0cd266be5aacdd9f165d173bb1ea34766d371a1a380255f0c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-38596/selection/43cccfa7afd1786868b5663386d0851eab374d8c0f6befd3946896f45ba661d0" "q-38596/selection/b72dd9697f49385ccc5e5960ffb4cca18179ab08897d5d50eda25d57fed380f3" "q-38596/selection/c10de62d8125dd952ae2853436204c7ac91ef2cf9c24ef921872a8506d65eb0b" "q-38596/selection/0a699f5e222b2541cc0b57d0909108bee4edcc63642004a89241b5631a6dad5d" "q-38596/selection/468dcf99a9303f0cd266be5aacdd9f165d173bb1ea34766d371a1a380255f0c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38596" :question/id #uuid "3b568e1f-fb45-5c85-9ad6-367daab9d1a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38596" :question/problem "A bug population  $B$ increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the bug population at a given time. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the bug population $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*A **bug population** $B$ **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **bug population** $B$  at a given time.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *bug population* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *bug population.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{B}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the bug population *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{B}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38596/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
